==German==

===Etymology===
From Old French ''[[noix]] [[muscat]]'', from Middle Latin ''muscata'' "nutmeg", from Greek ''moschos'' "[[musk]]".  Here is the real explanation...  Nuss is to Nuesse as Muss is to Muesse.  Cata means something else entirely.  Look at Muscat, Oman.

